@Focus:
- **Device Authorization Button Flow (2026-08-15):** Phases 4 + 5 of the soulbits-cloud-backend device-auth-button-flow workstream. (1) `soulbits://` CUSTOM SCHEME — `soulbits://device-auth?code=<6-digit>` deep link handled in new `src/services/cloud/deviceDeepLink.ts`; per design it fires ONLY from the portal page in a browser, never from the email body (immune to mail clients stripping custom schemes; no assetlinks/apple-app-site-association infra). (2) CLIENT PIN BUMP — `@harmony-ai-solutions/soulbits-api-client` re-pinned to the pushed commit `cb85ec9` (git+ssh GitHub dependency, `prepare` builds tsup dist). (3) MODAL POLLING + AUTO-CONTINUE — `DeviceAuthModal` polls `GET /v1/devices/authorize/status` every 5 s while visible; when `authorized` flips true it closes itself and retries the cloud connect; the manual 6-digit code entry stays as fallback. i18n copy in `auth.json` + tests (`DeviceAuthModal.render.test.tsx`, `deviceDeepLink.test.ts`, `deviceAuth.test.ts`). All UNCOMMITTED with the rest of the phase stack. Verification: `npx tsc --noEmit` 0 errors; jest unit 71 suites / 611 tests green.
- **Character Profile Editor — Desktop-UI Parity Alignment (2026-08-11):** Brought the RN character profile editor to parity with the Wails frontend's recent layout/i18n changes (the 7-bullet editor feedback + lifecycle editor port). (1) SECTION REORDER in `src/screens/CharacterProfileEditScreen.tsx`: Identity → Voice & Persona → Images (now 2nd, was last) → Greeting → Scenario → Lorebook → Lifecycle (NEW) → Advanced → Attribution (now last). (2) LOREBOOK ENTRY EDITOR (`src/components/character-card/LorebookEntryEditor.tsx`): removed the Advanced (export-only spec fields: position, insertion_order, priority, selective/secondary keys, case_sensitive, use_regex, id) section from the UI; reordered to Name/Comment → Content → Keys → Matching (enabled + constant). Advanced fields carried verbatim from the seeded draft on save for card round-trip parity with Wails (removed now-unused state: advancedOpen, secondaryKeysText, position, insertionOrderText, priorityText, idText + POSITIONS const). (3) NEW RN `src/components/character-card/LifecycleConfigEditor.tsx` — full port of the Wails editor: 5 sections (Beat Schedule, Sleep & Exhaustion, Emotion Decay, Crystallization, Memory) with autonomy chips + numeric TextInputs + per-field detailed hints. Mobile-native collapsible section info: each section header has a ⓘ icon; tap → expand a bordered description card inline (no portal needed — it expands within the scroll, sidestepping the Wails overflow:hidden + backdrop-filter clipping issue entirely). Exports `LifecycleConfig` interface + `LifecycleConfigEditor` component. (4) i18n `src/i18n/locales/en/characters.json`: `advanced` "Advanced" → "AI Behaviour"; new `lifecycleSection` = "AI Lifecycle"; + full nested `lifecycle.*` block (52 keys, verbatim from Wails — defaultsNote, 5 section groups with title/tooltip + per-field label/unit/hint, autonomyLevels enum, beatTypes map). (5) LIFECYCLE WIRING in the screen: new `lifecycleConfig` state (`useState<LifecycleConfig>({})`); `loadProfile` parses `profile.lifecycle_config` JSON via `parseJsonColumn<LifecycleConfig>`; `buildProfileFields` now includes `lifecycle_config: JSON.stringify(lifecycleConfig)`; removed the create call's hardcoded `lifecycle_config: '{}'` and the export's (now flows through buildProfileFields); defaults banner (accent-tinted card, info icon + `lifecycle.defaultsNote`) above the editor. VERIFICATION: `npx tsc --noEmit` exit 0; JSON valid; 48 static lifecycle literals resolve, 0 missing (4 dynamic `${type}`/`${lvl}` template keys excluded from the literal check); section order confirmed via grep (10 sections in target order). SENJU BRANCH CLASH CHECK (`senju-design-updates`, 18 commits — personas + Discover/Market refactor): touches `CharacterProfileEditScreen.tsx` ONLY in imports + the create-on-save path (+3 lines, `setCharacterProfileSource(newId,'user')`) — non-overlapping with our JSX/state/section work; does NOT touch `LorebookEntryEditor.tsx` or `characters.json`; heavily rewrites `characters.ts` (+170 — AVOIDED; lifecycle persisted via existing full-object `updateCharacterProfile` spread, no repo edit). No migration needed (lifecycle_config column already exists). tsc clean. Changelog updated. NOT yet device-verified.
- **My Profile Screen + Persona System (2026-08-10):** Per user request, the My Profile tab is now a complete professional profile. Layout: ScreenHeader (title + hamburger) -> hero (gradient-ring ProfileAvatar 112dp, bold display name, small NON-bold muted @username directly underneath) -> Edit Profile button (ThemedButton secondary -> EditProfile) -> stats ThemedCard (Followers 0 | Following 0 | AI Characters = count of getUserCharacterProfiles()) -> bio ThemedCard -> ProfileTabs segmented control (AI Characters | Posts | Saved; Posts/Saved = ThemedEmptyState) -> Personas section (SectionHeader + "New Persona" pill + ThemedCard of PersonaRows). All data is LOCAL-FIRST: cloud useAuth().user (base UserProfile now has OPTIONAL username/bio/avatar_url fields - backend /v1/auth/me does not return them yet) is merged with per-user AsyncStorage extras via new src/services/profile/UserProfileStore.ts (key @harmony_profile/<userId>, stores displayName/username/bio/avatar_data_url; MyProfileScreen resolves displayName as local displayName || cloud user.display_name || 'User', and EditProfileScreen persists the edited display name locally since there is no backend PATCH /v1/auth/me yet). New screens: src/screens/EditProfileScreen.tsx (display name, username with @ prefix, bio, avatar picker via launchImageLibrary inside withExternalFlow; saves via UserProfileStore) and src/screens/PersonaEditScreen.tsx (create/edit a persona = Entity + linked CharacterProfile tagged source='user'; fields name/description/personality/picture; create path generates generateId() profile + entity alias=name with UNIQUE-alias conflict guard, setCharacterProfileSource(profileId,'user'), empty module mapping, syncService.syncAndWait best-effort before goBack; edit path updateCharacterProfile + updateEntity + primary-image replace/remove via deleteCharacterImage+createCharacterImage; delete path deleteEntity). Both routes registered in AppNavigator (EditProfile: undefined, PersonaEdit: {entityId?: string} | undefined); MainTabs now typed NavigatorScreenParams<MainTabParamList> | undefined. New shared components: src/components/profile/ProfileAvatar.tsx (gradient-ring avatar with initials fallback), PersonaRow.tsx (avatar/name/desc + ACTIVE chip + chat-as button + chevron), ProfileTabs.tsx (segmented pills). New repo fns: getUserPersonas/getPersonaByEntityId in src/database/repositories/personas.ts (entities INNER JOIN character_profiles INNER JOIN character_profile_sources WHERE source='user', avatar via getPrimaryImage+imageToDataURL) and getUserCharacterProfiles in characters.ts (mirrors getCommunityCharacterProfiles with INNER JOIN source='user'). Persona "chat as" button calls ChatPreferencesService.setGlobalImpersonatedEntity + updates the ACTIVE chip + shows toast - re-introducing the persona selector removed from ChatList header on this screen. SIGN-IN REDIRECT: AuthContext gained signInVersion (monotonic counter bumped after login/loginWithGoogle/loginWithApple only - NOT on bootstrap/refresh), exposed in the context value; App.tsx AppShell observes it via a prevSignInVersionRef and on change navigationRef.navigate('MainTabs', { screen: 'MyProfile' }) (100ms delay) so a fresh sign-in lands the user on their profile. Unauthenticated state: MyProfile tab shows ThemedEmptyState + "Sign In" button -> Login. i18n: profile.json expanded with all hero/stats/tabs/persona/edit keys. Changelog updated (new "Profile" section). tsc --noEmit clean; unit 46 suites / 438 tests green; NOT yet device-verified; no unit tests reference the new screens.
- **Chat List — "Chatting as" Pill + Identity-Settings Button Removed (2026-08-10):** Per user request, removed BOTH the "Chatting as" persona pill (with its gradient-ring avatar, name, chevron, `ImpersonationSelectorModal` trigger) AND the adjacent identity-settings ⚙ cog button (`edit-my-identity-button` → `EntityConfigEdit`) from the ChatListScreen header. PRESERVED for later re-introduction on another screen: `src/components/modals/ImpersonationSelectorModal.tsx`, `HeaderMenuButton` (still in the header), `ChatPreferencesService`, the i18n keys in `chatList.json` (`chattingAs`, `editMyIdentity`, `editIdentityAction`), and the underlying global impersonation state. `ChatListScreen` still loads the stored persona (`loadImpersonatedEntity` + `ChatPreferencesService.getGlobalImpersonatedEntity`) and drives the conversation list with it — only the header UI entry points are gone. Removed dead code: `ImpersonationSelectorModal` import/render, `handleImpersonationSelect`, `handleEditMyIdentity`, `selectorModalVisible`, `impersonatedEntityDisplay` state, and the `impersonationPill*`/`myIdentityButton` styles. tsc clean; no tests reference the removed test IDs. Changelog updated (Navigation > Changed). The persona selector will live on a future screen (e.g. Settings).
- **Unified Empty-State Design Across App (2026-08-10):** All "nothing here yet"/0-results/not-paired/empty states now share the Market screen's premium design via a new shared component `src/components/themed/ThemedEmptyState.tsx` — gradient icon ring (`ThemedGradient primary` + elevated inner circle) with bold title + muted hint + optional action. Applied to: CharactersScreen (no profiles / no results), DiscoverScreen (no characters / no results — overlay), ChatListScreen (no conversations / not-paired / cloud-preparing), EntityConfigScreen (no entities), EmojiActionEditorScreen (no actions), EmojiGrid (emoji search 0-results, compact). MarketScreen refactored to consume the same component. All states are consistently sized and positioned right below the header (removed `justifyContent:'center'` from `emptyListContent` in Characters/EntityConfig so they sit at the top like Market instead of vertically centered). Supports `testID`/`accessibilityLabel` passthrough (kept `chat-list-empty`, `chat-list-not-paired`, `chat-list-cloud-preparing`, `open-connection-manager-button`, `connect-now-button` for Maestro). tsc --noEmit clean; no unit tests reference these screens. Changelog updated (Navigation > Changed).
- **Settings Moved Out of Tab Bar → Header Hamburger Menu (2026-08-10):** The Settings entry is no longer a bottom tab. Removed the `Settings` route from `MainTabNavigator` + `GlassTabBar` (TAB_ICONS/FALLBACK_LABELS) — the tab bar is now 4 items: Chat | Discover [CENTER] | Characters | Market. `SettingsScreen` is now a root-stack route in `AppNavigator` (pushed over the tabs, gets a back button via `ScreenHeader onBack`). New `src/components/navigation/HeaderMenuButton.tsx` renders a compact obsidian-glass circular "three lines" (☰) button (accent lines on glass pill, haptic + theme-aware). Tapping it navigates DIRECTLY to the full `SettingsScreen` (per user request — the old `SettingsMenu` modal was deleted as "the shitty old window"). `HeaderMenuButton` is mounted in the header (`ScreenHeader right`) of all 4 tab screens: ChatList (in the existing header-right row), Discover, Characters, and Market. The orphaned `navigation` i18n namespace was also removed (its only consumer `SettingsMenu` was deleted; `navigation.json` deleted + `I18nContext` cleaned). E2E: `_shared/navigate-to-sync-settings.yaml` now taps `header-menu-button` → `settings-sync-card` (was `tab-settings` + `settings-sync-card`). Docs updated: CHANGELOG (Navigation > Changed), .planning/codebase ARCHITECTURE+STRUCTURE, reports. tsc --noEmit clean; no unit tests reference GlassTabBar/SettingsMenu.
- **Discover — Other-Users'-Characters Grid + Search (2026-08-10):** Discover now shows ONLY AI characters created by OTHER users (those synced DOWN from the engine — they arrive with no source tag → default 'community'). The CURRENT user's own characters — created via Create AI, the profile editor, or imported character cards — are tagged 'user' and hidden from their own Discover (they still sync UP to the engine and appear on other users' Discover grids). Because `getChangedRecords` reads `character_profiles` via `SELECT *` and syncs all columns to the engine (strict schema parity per docs/schema-parity.md), a `source` column on character_profiles would break parity — so source tracking lives in a CLIENT-ONLY sidecar table `character_profile_sources` (migration 000035 creates the table; 000036 backfills pre-existing profiles as 'user' so existing installs hide their current characters). New repo fns in `src/database/repositories/characters.ts`: `setCharacterProfileSource`, `getCharacterProfileSource`, `getCommunityCharacterProfiles` (LEFT JOIN sidecar, filters out 'user'). `CreateAIScreen` + `CharacterProfileEditScreen` (create path) + `CharacterCardImportService` (import path) all call `setCharacterProfileSource(profileId, 'user')` after creation; ONLY the sync-down path stays untagged → community. DiscoverScreen loads via `getCommunityCharacterProfiles` (not `getAllCharacterProfiles`), searches by NAME only (case-insensitive; description matching was removed because long descriptions matched almost any letter and hid the 0-results state), and renders a guaranteed-visible overlay (NOT ListEmptyComponent — unreliable with numColumns>1) for loading/0-results/empty states. i18n `discover.json`: searchPlaceholder, noResults("No results found for \"{{query}}\""), noResultsHint, noCharacters("No characters to discover yet"), noCharactersHint("Characters created by other users will show up here."), chatOpenFailed. Schema parity: `scripts/dump-schema.ts` now excludes CLIENT_ONLY_TABLES (`character_profile_sources`) from the RN dump so the RN↔Go parity gate stays green; `schema/rn-schema.json` regenerated. Characters tab unchanged (shows everything incl. user-created). Migration snapshots updated; tsc clean; unit 46 suites green (intermittent better-sqlite3 cross-worker flakes in nodeSide/nodeDatabase.smoke/cross-repo are pre-existing and pass in isolation/reruns). Changelog updated under Navigation > Changed.
- **Search Tab Merged Into Discover (2026-08-10):** Removed the dedicated Search tab (SearchScreen.tsx + search.json + tab-search testID + nav.search i18n key) per user request. The Discover tab (`src/screens/DiscoverScreen.tsx`) now renders a glass search bar injected into the ScreenHeader and a 2-column grid of AI character profiles (same `CharacterProfileCard` + `getAllCharacterProfiles`/`getCharacterImages` repos as CharactersScreen), filtered live by name/description. Tapping a card opens `CharacterProfileEdit`, and the card's chat button runs the full `CharactersScreen.handleChatPress` flow (resolve impersonated entity → reuse/create entity via `getEntityByCharacterProfileId` → `syncService.syncAndWait` on new entities → derive participantKey/scope → navigate to ChatDetail with temp UUIDv7). 4-tab bar now: Discover | Chat [CENTER] | Characters | Settings — GlassTabBar TAB_ICONS/FALLBACK_LABELS, MainTabParamList, SettingsMenu nav item, and I18nContext (import/resource/ns) all updated. i18n: discover.json gained searchPlaceholder/noResults/noResultsHint/noCharacters/noCharactersHint/chatOpenFailed; navigation.json dropped nav.search. Comments + codebase maps (.planning) + reports updated. tsc --noEmit clean; unit 44 suites pass (2 pre-existing DB rollback test suites failing — unrelated). Changelog updated under Navigation > Changed.
- **Module Config — Simplified UX + Soulbits Cloud Consistency (2026-08-08, Task 3 of Dom's feedback):** Three items on `ModuleConfigEditScreen` + constants. (1) PROVIDER LIST AUDIT — `src/constants/moduleConfiguration.ts`: added `soulbitscloud` to the RAG, STT, and TTS `providerOptions` (they were missing it even though the model catalog supports embeddings/whisper/tts models; regression guard in new `moduleConfiguration.test.ts` asserts every module with a `SOULBITS_MODEL_QUERY` also lists Soulbits Cloud). (2) VAD MODEL MAPPING — new `vad` entry in `SOULBITS_MODEL_QUERY` (`model_type: 'vad'`) + `SOULBITS_FALLBACK_MODELS.vad = ['silero-vad']` (real live-catalog id); `renderInlineProviderFields` now resolves the model-select module type via `modelModuleType = slot === 'vad' ? 'vad' : moduleType` so the VAD slot queries voice-activity models instead of STT transcription models. (3) CONDITIONAL FIELD VISIBILITY — when a managed Soulbits Cloud provider is selected AND the app is in cloud mode (`connectionStatus.mode === 'cloud'`), the endpoint (`base_url`/`endpoint`) and credential (`api_key`/`api_token`) fields are HIDDEN in both Simple and Advanced modes (auto-synced from backend; injected via `injectSoulbitsToken`, synced via `soulbitsTokenSync`). New pure helper module `src/constants/moduleConfigVisibility.ts` (`isSimpleFieldKey`, `isManagedCloudField`, `SIMPLE_FIELD_KEYS`) unit-tested. (4) SIMPLE VS ADVANCED TOGGLE — COMPACT SEGMENTED CONTROL (Simple | Advanced pills, accent-filled active segment) in a slim card below General (FOLLOW-UP: user rejected the first full-card chevron toggle as "ugly + buggy" — the bug was a side-effect inside the state updater; fixed by persisting via a separate `useEffect([showAdvanced])`). Simple mode shows only `SIMPLE_FIELD_KEYS` (name/credentials/endpoint/model/voice/speed/format…) + hides `AdvancedSamplingParams`; Advanced mode shows the full schema. Preference persisted in AsyncStorage key `module_config_show_advanced` (restored on mount, written on toggle). i18n keys `modeLabel`/`modeSimple`/`modeAdvanced`/`modeSimpleHint`/`modeAdvancedHint` in `moduleConfig.json`. (5) PLUS-BUTTON REMOVAL (FOLLOW-UP: user disliked the trailing "+" per module selector) — `EntityModuleSelectorWithActions` no longer renders a create "+" button; `EntityModuleSelector` gained an optional `onCreateNew` prop that renders a "Create new config…" row as the last sheet item (plus-circle-outline icon, accent), and only the pencil edit button remains beside the selector when a config is selected. Verification: tsc clean; unit 46 suites / 430 tests green (new: `moduleConfigVisibility.test.ts` 5, `moduleConfiguration.test.ts` 3, `soulbitsModels.test.ts` +vad cases); integration 9 suites / 46 pass + 1 skip; eslint only pre-existing 3 errors (exhaustive-deps ×2, unused `moduleSpecificDefaults`) + 6 inline-style warnings (3 pre-existing in EntityModuleSelector). Changelog updated. NOT yet device-verified; no test files render ModuleConfigEditScreen or the selectors.
- **Characters Screen — Chat Button on Character Cards (2026-08-08):** Each `CharacterProfileCard` on the Characters screen now shows a floating chat button (accent gradient pill, top-right over the portrait) that opens a direct chat with that character. ChatDetail requires an ENTITY linked to the character profile plus the impersonated "user" entity, so `CharactersScreen.handleChatPress` resolves the global impersonated entity (same logic as CreateAIScreen), looks up an entity via the new repository function `getEntityByCharacterProfileId` (returns most-recently-created active entity; added to `src/database/repositories/entities.ts` with 4 unit tests), and if none exists creates one (id + alias = profile name, links `character_profile_id`, empty module mapping) and AWAITS `syncService.syncAndWait` before navigating (engine must ingest the entity before INIT_ENTITY or chat sticks on "Connecting..."). Then derives participantKey via `deriveParticipantKey`/`deriveScopeFromParticipants`, generates a temp UUIDv7 interactionId (ChatDetail replaces it with the canonical server ID) and navigates to `ChatDetail`. The card button stops press propagation so it never triggers the card's edit/long-press handlers. i18n `chatOpenFailed` added to characters.json. tsc clean; unit 44 suites / 421 tests green (4 new for the repository lookup). Changelog updated. NOT yet device-verified; no test files reference CharactersScreen.
- **Create AI — Visual Profile Picker Carousel (2026-08-08):** Per Dom's feedback, the "create a character from an existing profile" flow no longer uses a plain text dropdown (avatar only appeared after selection — felt like picking a DB row). Replaced with a horizontal card carousel in the Character Profile card on `CreateAIScreen`: each card (`src/components/characters/ProfilePickerCard.tsx`) mirrors the Obsidian Glass anatomy of `CharacterProfileCard` (Characters screen) — 3:4 portrait with dark fade overlay, theme-glass body, hairline gradient border that becomes a 2px accent ring when selected, ambient glow (intensified when selected), name + description snippet, left accent stripe, plus a check badge on the selected card. The "Create new profile" card is the first item with a ＋ placeholder. All profiles' primary images are now loaded up front into a `profileImages` map (was: only the selected profile's image was fetched after selection) so avatars show BEFORE confirming. Selecting a card prefills Name/Personality and centers the hero preview; the carousel auto-scrolls to center the selected card on layout (ref + `scrollToIndex`, `onScrollToIndexFailed` guard). Switching back to "Create new profile" resets the prefilled identity fields (name/personality) — fixed a regression where the previously selected card's name stuck around. Removed the bottom-sheet Modal + its styles. New i18n key `createNewProfileHint`. tsc clean; eslint only pre-existing warning. Changelog updated. NOT yet device-verified; no test files reference CreateAIScreen.
- **Chat Lifecycle — Stuck-"connecting" Strand + Monkey Test (2026-08-05, on-device-diagnosed):** Re-test after Fix A (dedup) + Fix C (participant-set connection ids) confirmed both working (single sync per switch, less flaky, distinct `entity-user-<pk>` sockets). Residual: a Marcella session briefly stuck in "connecting" ~15s then resolved via the init retry. Root cause (adb timeline): `INIT_ENTITY SUCCESS` for the partner entity arrived BEFORE `startInteractionSession` registered the session in `this.sessions` (registration was AFTER the parallel connect+send `Promise.all`); `handleEntityEvent → handleInitEntityResponse` then ran with `interactionSession === null`, so the connection was never marked 'active' → the session never reached all-active → stalled until the 15s init timer retried. FIX: moved `this.sessions.set(tempInteractionId, session)` to BEFORE the parallel send loop (connections map is shared by ref, so entries added below stay visible) + `this.sessions.delete(tempInteractionId)` in the catch on failure. Added a deterministic seeded "monkey" stress test `entitySessionMonkey.test.ts` (40 rapid Marcella↔Claire switches, simulated backend responds ~50% SYNCHRONOUSLY during sendEvent + 50% via randomized timers — the sync case is the race window). Invariant: exactly one `session:started` per start + no leaks + no throws. COUNTER-TEST PROVEN by user request: with the fix reverted the monkey test FAILS (9/40 starts completed — the rest stranded); with the fix restored it PASSES (40/40). This validates both the strand fix AND the dedup guard (double-emit would exceed 40). Unit 43→44 suites / 416→417 tests; tsc clean; `--maxWorkers` 45 still ≥ 44. UNCOMMITTED (user staged the prior work).
- **Chat Lifecycle — Duplicate session:started + Participant-Set Connection IDs (2026-08-05, on-device-diagnosed Fixes A & C):** On-device re-test of the cascade fix (above) surfaced two NEW interaction-session bugs (distinct from the cascade, which is fixed — no crash/ping-pong/retry-loop). (A) DUPLICATE `session:started` → double sync per chat-open: `EntitySessionService.handleInitEntityResponse` emitted `session:started` (+ the on-start `initiateSync`) with NO guard; both participants' INIT_ENTITY SUCCESS responses raced through the own-entity's `await createInteraction(...)` window and BOTH re-entered the all-active check after both connections were already 'active' → emit twice + 2 syncs (adb: `session:started`→`Initiating sync`×2, 1ms apart). FIX: added `InteractionSession.started` flag, emit/sync only when `allActive && !started`. (C) `entity-${entityId}` COLLISION across participant sets: the engine keys sessions by participant set (one canonical interaction_id per distinct participant set — user's earlier engine fix), but the app used a single `entity-user` slot for every chat → rapid Marcella↔Claire switching raced the previous `entity-user` teardown against the new `entity-user` setup → native "Already Connected"/stale-socket → 15s init timeouts → "Scheduling retry 1/3…3/3" connection delay. FIX: connection id now `entity-${entityId}-${participantKey}` (participantKey from deriveParticipantKey, '+' sanitized to '-' for URL safety in `?connection_id=`); `ConnectionManager.getEntityConnection` (unused) switched to scan by stored entityId. Event routing unaffected (uses ConnectionInfo.entityId, not id parsing). B (sync-on-start + sync-on-message) is INTENTIONAL per user — tuning is a separate concern. D (session-map isolation on canonical-id reuse) deferred per user ("not necessary once A lands") — rundown provided. Tests: new `entitySessionStartedDedup.test.ts` (2) + `entitySessionConnectionId.test.ts` (2); unit 41→43 suites / 412→416 tests; tsc clean; `--maxWorkers` 45 still ≥ 43. UNCOMMITTED with the cascade fix.
- **Chat Cascade Fix — Sibling Connection Coverage + Timeout-Branch Hardening (2026-08-05 follow-up):** Code review of the cascade fix (next bullet) confirmed the bug class is UNIQUE to the self-signed native module — the 3 sibling WS modes (`Unencrypted`/`Secure`/`Cloud`) use the standard browser `new WebSocket(url)` API (no listener-overwrite-without-unsubscribe, no synthetic close-error on a dead socket, no per-URL `getInstance` singleton) so they need NO equivalent fix; entity+sync both route through `InsecureSSLWebSocketConnection` for the local self-signed engine (entity mode = `ConnectionStateManager.getSecurityMode()`, same as sync). Filled the prior test-coverage GAP: new `src/services/websocket/__tests__/helpers/MockWebSocket.ts` (browser-style WS mock with `OPEN/CONNECTING/CLOSING/CLOSED` statics, `fire*` test helpers, real-`setImmediate` `flushMicrotasks()` that survives `jest.useFakeTimers()`) + 3 new suites — `UnencryptedWebSocketConnection.test.ts` (8: connect/error/reconnect-replace/server-close/send-guard/disconnect), `SecureWebSocketConnection.test.ts` (6: JWT subprotocol, missing-JWT, cert-vs-generic error routing, 10s timeout, reconnect), `CloudWebSocketConnection.test.ts` (7: PASETO subprotocol, not-authenticated, connect-failure-rejects-WITHOUT-disconnected, 1008 auth-refresh, established close, 15s timeout, settled-guard-no-double-settle). HARDENED observation 1 (was a bounded wart): the InsecureSSL `connect()` timeout branch settled the promise WITHOUT marking `failureSignalled`, so a delayed native onError leaked one extra `error`; root cause was SCOPE — `failureSignalled` was declared inside the `try` block (invisible to the timeout callback in the outer Promise-executor scope). Hoisted the declaration into the executor scope and set it in the timeout branch → timeout/onError/.catch now share ONE settle guard. New InsecureSSL characterization test pins it (timeout rejects exactly once, late error suppressed, next connect recovers). Impact analysis: LOW (interface-dispatched; 2 connection-establishment processes). Unit 38→41 suites / 390→412 tests; `--maxWorkers` bumped 40→45 in `package.json` + `docs/TESTING.md` (41 unit files now exceeds the documented 40-file better-sqlite3 cross-worker contamination threshold); tsc clean; `npm run test:unit` green.
- **Chat Connection Cascade Fix — Session-Stop Leak + WS Error Ping-Pong Crash (2026-08-05, logcat+docker-diagnosed):** User report: after the engine-side participant-matching fix, Marcella chat worked but Claire chat stuck in "Connecting...", then retries + error toast, escalating to an app crash. Diagnosed via adb logcat + docker logs + code: FOUR interacting app-side bugs. (1) TRIGGER — connection leak on chat exit: `EntitySessionService.stopInteractionSession` ran `await AudioPlayer.stop()` FIRST in its try-block; it throws `player_not_initialized` when TrackPlayer was never set up (no audio played in that chat) → outer catch swallowed → connection-teardown loop NEVER ran → every chat exit leaked its entity WebSockets ("Connection entity-X already exists, disconnecting first" on next session; "Received event for unknown entity" heartbeats on session-less connections; orphaned engine-side sessions). FIX: AudioPlayer.stop isolated in its own try/catch + per-connection fault isolation in the teardown loop. (2) AMPLIFIER/CRASH — `react-native-websocket-self-signed` JS `onX()` methods overwrite `listeners[event]` WITHOUT removing the previous native subscription; `InsecureSSLWebSocketConnection` "cleared" handlers by registering no-ops → orphaned real closures kept answering native onError with `ws.close()`; native `close()` on a missing socket emits ANOTHER `onError("No active WebSocket for this URL")` → self-sustaining ping-pong flood (2 events → hundreds/sec) → JNI global-ref table overflow (`art::JavaVMExt::AddGlobalRef` abort) = the crash. Same mechanism killed fresh sockets mid-handshake ("Socket is closed" on entity-user) — why Claire's connect failed instantly while Marcella (fewer orphans then) squeaked through. FIX: remove-then-register (`removeOn*Listener()`) in the connect prologue + after getInstance; benign "No active WebSocket for this URL" ignored (no close/emit/reject); `failureSignalled` guard dedups error emit+close per connect attempt. USER CONSTRAINT: never edit node_modules (no patch-package) — residual native quirks (no onClosed map cleanup → "Already Connected" costs one extra retry; close() on missing socket emits onError) mitigated JS-side; upstream patch documented in docs/future-work.md #24. (3) LOOP — retry counter wipe: the `preserveRetryState` fix only covered the clear in `startInteractionSession`; `retryInitialization`'s cleanup `stopInteractionSession` unconditionally deleted the participant-key retry state ("Cancelled pending fallback retry") → counter reset → "Scheduling retry 1/3" forever (~110 cycles/2min hammering the engine with connect/disconnect). FIX: snapshot/restore retry state around the cleanup stop. (4) Tests: new `entitySessionStop.test.ts` (AudioPlayer throw still disconnects all + per-conn fault isolation), InsecureSSL suite rewritten (self-firing fake: default connect fires captured onOpen + resolves) + 4 new regression tests, retry suite +1 (lingering-session cleanup path — reproduces the exact device flow). Unit: 38 suites / 390 tests green; tsc clean. GitNexus detect_changes: 3 expected processes only. UNCOMMITTED. Device verify pending: rebuild → Marcella↔Claire switching, watch logcat for absent "No active WebSocket" flood + escalating "Scheduling retry 2/3…3/3" then give-up.
- **Sync Name-Clash Keep ID-Cascade + stt_configs Dual-Provider Fix (2026-08-04, DEVICE-VERIFIED):** Three sequential device/test-reported bugs in the name-clash "keep" path, all fixed TDD and confirmed working on the emulator by the user ("sync fix works now with the ID rewrite").
  - **Bug 1 — keep never re-sent the adopted record.** `applyIdAdoption` (keep branch, `SyncService.ts`) adopted the server id into the local module-config row but the SQL only set `id` — no `updated_at` bump and provider_config_id still pointed at the LOCAL provider id. App's ONLY dirty-tracking is `getChangedRecords` (created_at/updated_at/deleted_at > lastSync) → row stayed invisible → never pushed; the `serverRecordIds` filter would also suppress it. Pulled the emulator DB (`ai.soulbits.chat.dev`, `harmony.db` via `adb exec-out run-as ... cat` — PS redirection corrupts binaries) — kept rows still showed the original 21:14:17Z `updated_at`. FIX: keep branch now `UPDATE ... SET id=?, updated_at=?, provider_config_id=?` (per ref) AND keep-resolved keys are DELETED from `serverRecordIds` after commit so the record re-sends as `update`. New integration test: `keep re-sends the adopted record with a bumped updated_at and the server provider_config_id`.
  - **Bug 2 — keep did not cascade to the app's local provider configs.** "keep" must preserve the COMPLETE app setup (module config + its provider config); IDs must match the incoming data so it can sync back. First draft (copy local values ONTO the server provider row + hard-delete the local row) FAILED in the test harness: NodeDatabase executes statements synchronously but defers success callbacks to microtasks → nested-callback SELECT/UPDATE/DELETE ran after COMMIT → "Failed to apply server data". REDESIGNED to RENAME semantics (per user's clarifying question): `cascadeKeepProviderConfig` RENAMES the LOCAL `provider_config_*` row to the server provider-config id (values + created_at preserved), bumps updated_at, SKIPS the incoming duplicate via `keptProviderServerIds` (rename can't collide on PK), re-points remaining module-config refs, re-sends the provider config. `keepCascadedProviderKeys` Set (cleared in `initiateSync` + on rollback; keys un-excluded from `serverRecordIds` post-commit). All cascade SQL issued SYNCHRONOUSLY inside the tx — no callback nesting; local provider refs are CAPTURED pre-transaction in `buildApplyPlan` from `clash.localRecord` (no in-transaction SELECT). Test: `keep renames the local provider config to the server id and re-sends it`.
  - **Bug 3 — device `failed to apply server data`: `stt_configs` has NO `provider_config_id` column.** Live adb logcat showed `SQLiteException: no such column: provider_config_id ... UPDATE stt_configs SET provider_config_id = ?` → whole apply tx rolled back. PRAGMA table_info on the pulled device DB: `stt_configs` has TWO provider refs — `transcription_provider`/`transcription_provider_config_id` AND `vad_provider`/`vad_provider_config_id` (all NOT NULL). My earlier schema check used a naive regex that falsely matched the `…_provider_config_id` SUBSTRING. FIX: `PROVIDER_CONFIG_REFERENCES` per-table map in `syncNameClash.ts` (`stt_configs` → both transcription+vad pairs; the other 7 module-config tables → single `provider_config_id`/`provider`); `NameClashApplyDirective` keep variant now carries `providerRefs: ReadonlyArray<KeepProviderRefCapture>` = `{configColumn, providerColumn, localProviderConfigId, localProvider}`; `applyIdAdoption` builds a per-ref UPDATE + `keptProviderServerIds` from the captured refs; `cascadeKeepProviderConfig` remap loop iterates the map (both stt columns). Engine `stt_configs` schema (migration 000031) confirmed IDENTICAL — incoming records carry the same columns. Regression test: `keep cascades BOTH stt_configs provider references (transcription + vad) to the server ids and re-sends them` (reproduces the device failure; would hit "no such column" pre-fix).
  - Verification: unit 377/377 (35 suites — `--maxWorkers` bumped 16→40 in package.json + docs/TESTING.md when the 35th unit file crossed the documented better-sqlite3 cross-worker contamination threshold); integration 46 pass + 1 skip (9 suites); name-clash suite 12 tests; tsc clean. All UNCOMMITTED with the rest of the name-clash WIP.
- **Sync Name-Clash Resolution Feature (2026-08-04):** Engine re-sends module-config rows (same `name`, different UUID) after an engine-side seed/restore or second device creates them; on the app the incoming INSERT would violate the DB-level UNIQUE name constraint → sync transaction abort → permanent "failed to apply server data" loop. Implemented app-side clash resolution: `src/services/syncNameClash.ts` (pure) + wiring in `SyncService.ts` (applyBufferedSyncData → buildApplyPlan → resolveNameClash) + `SyncSettingsScreen` dialog (`sync:name_clash` event, "Apply to all" checkbox). Modes: **overwrite** (server wins — adopt server id + values, remap local refs), **keep** (app wins — adopt server id, keep local values, remap refs, re-send; see cascade entry above), **rename** (local keeps its id, renamed `"X (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS)"` via `generateRenamedName`, server record inserted). Clash detection spans the 8 `NAME_UNIQUE_TABLES` (backend/cognition/movement/rag/stt/tts/vision/imagination configs) + `CONFIG_ID_REFERENCES` (module configs referencing provider_config_id, entities.character_profile_id, character_profiles.vision_config_id). Migration 000034: rebuild `vision_configs` + `imagination_configs` with `name TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` (the 6 others already enforced it) — `_new`-table rebuild wrapped in `PRAGMA foreign_keys=OFF/ON` because `character_profiles.vision_config_id` FK (ON DELETE SET NULL) would fire on a plain DROP TABLE; mirrors harmony-link-private migration 000034 (schema parity; the migration runner disables FKs on HL too). Unit `syncNameClash.test.ts` + 12 integration tests.
- **AppAlert Popup Race Guard (2026-08-04):** Observed popup vanishing on fast dismiss/replace — `AppAlertContext.handleDismiss` ran `setTimeout(() => setConfig(null), 200)` and unconditionally cleared whatever config was current when the timer fired (e.g. a NEW alert opened within 200ms was wiped). Fix: generation guard — capture `dismissedConfig = pendingRef.current` at dismiss time; the delayed `setConfig(null)` only runs if `pendingRef.current === dismissedConfig`. Tests: `AppAlertContext.test.tsx` 2/2 green (debug mock marker later removed).
- **updated_at Bump on All Config Updates — Sync Dirty-Tracking Fix (2026-08-04):** Cross-repo fix with harmony-link-private. Root cause of "API key edits never reach the engine" (engine kept returning 401 "authorization header required" on all SoulbitsCloud calls): the app's ONLY change detection is `getChangedRecords` (`database/sync.ts`) — selects rows where `created_at`/`updated_at`/`deleted_at` > lastSync — but `update<Provider>Config` and `update<Module>Config` SQL never set `updated_at`, so edited rows stayed invisible to sync and were never pushed. Fixed: appended `updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP` to the SET clause of ALL 16 `update<Provider>Config` functions (`src/database/repositories/providers/*.ts`: openai, ollama, openaicompatible, openrouter, harmonyspeech, elevenlabs, kindroid, kajiwoto, characterai, localai, mistral, comfyui, xai, google, anthropic, soulbitscloud) and all 8 `update<Module>Config` functions (`src/database/repositories/modules.ts`: backend, cognition, movement, rag, stt, tts, vision, imagination). NOT touched: `updateAllSoulbitsCloudApiKeys` (already bumps), create/delete/soft-delete paths, `sync.ts`, `SyncService.ts`. Tests (TDD red→green): `providers.test.ts` +5 (bumps updated_at for OpenAI/Ollama/Anthropic/SoulbitsCloud + end-to-end regression: backdated row NOT dirty before edit, IS dirty after), `modules.test.ts` +2 (backend + cognition). Unit: 33 suites / 366 tests green; eslint clean. Verified against live data: engine DB `provider_config_soulbitscloud.api_key` len 0 vs app DB len 53 (`sb_cloud_g*`) — identical rows/UUIDs (21:14:17). Engine-side companions (harmony-link-private): `syncProviderRecord` LWW tie-break (equal updated_at → incoming wins, matches app `>=`), cloud-mode seeder empty-token guard (was wiping keys + re-stamping updated_at at every boot without a token), entity-cache refresh after seed in `run.go`. Changes UNCOMMITTED alongside existing WIP — user to decide commit split.
- Sync Size-Estimate Confirmation + Toast-Suppression (2026-08-03): Cross-repo sync QoL work with harmony-link-private (engine). Three items:
  - (1) Engine size-estimate correctness (ENGINE repo): fixed the estimate/fetch mismatch — bare `strftime('%s', updated_at)` returned TEXT storage class so SQLite compared TEXT vs INTEGER watermark as "TEXT > any INTEGER" → every row counted (estimate said 7 records, fetch sent 0). Shared WHERE predicates `whereChangedSince`/`whereChangedSinceNoDeletedAt` in `database/sync_utils.go` now back all 32 `queryGetChanged*` fetch constants AND the counters (`CountChangedRecords` with internal table-name switch for 2-column `emotion_state` vs 3-column tables; `CountChangedCharacterImages` returns count+bytes). `sendSizeEstimate` covers all 33 tables incl. previously-missing `interactions`/`emotion_state`/`memories`; image-count query error no longer discarded. Verification: `go build ./...` + `go test ./database/ ./eventserver/` green (9/9 sync suite).
  - (2) Estimate confirmation protocol (ENGINE + APP): engine now BLOCKS after emitting `SYNC_DATA_SIZE_ESTIMATE` until the app replies with the new `SYNC_DATA_SIZE_ESTIMATE_CONFIRM` event (`{sync_session_id, event_id, status: SUCCESS|REJECTED}`), 60s timeout → engine sends `SYNC_REJECT` + aborts, NO data transmitted without confirmation. App-side: `SyncService.handleSizeEstimate`/`confirmSizeEstimate`/`pendingSizeEstimate` + new `sync:estimate`/`sync:estimate:confirm` events; `SyncConnectionContext` shows a themed dialog (Cancel→reject/Confirm→accept, `blockBackdropDismiss: true`) when the estimate exceeds the threshold or on initial sync. Empty estimates auto-confirm silently. Backward compatible (no estimate → sync proceeds as before).
  - (3) Toast suppression during expected handshake (APP): new pure gate `shouldShowConnectionErrorToast({isTransportSettled, isReconnecting, reconnectAttempt, isCertFlowActive})` in `syncSettlementHelper.ts` — never toasts on provisional/unsettled transports, during a cert-decision flow (cert modal is the intended UX), or inside the reconnect backoff loop (only the very first failure on a settled transport may toast). Wired into `SyncConnectionContext.handleSyncError` + `connect()` catch (new `isCertFlowActiveRef`, set on `cert:verification_failed` and before TLS dials, cleared on settled connect) and `ConnectionSetupScreen.handleConnectionError` (new `showCertModalRef` mirror). Kills the "connection error / connection dropped" toast spam during pairing when TLS/cert errors are expected. **Follow-up fix (on-device logs, adb logcat 08-03): a FOURTH ungated toast path remained — `ConnectionSetupScreen.handleHandshakeAccepted`'s catch showed "Failed to establish connection" whenever `attemptSecureConnection()` rethrew. Root cause: the failing connection is `InsecureSSLWebSocketConnection` (self-signed lib) which emits plain `'error'` (not `cert:verification_failed`), and `attemptSecureConnection`'s `isCertError` string check fails on the raw RN WS event (`{_defaultPrevented:false,_type:"error",...}` → no cert keywords) → rethrow → ungated toast. Log evidence: 08-02 builds toasted BOTH "Connection error occurred" AND "Failed to establish connection"; the 08-03 build suppressed the former (gate worked) but still fired the latter. Fixed by applying the SAME gate in that catch (`isCertFlowActive = showCertModalRef.current || !hasSelectedSecurityModeRef.current` — always true during pairing since `handleHandshakeAccepted` resets the ref to false → suppressed). New scenario test in `syncSettlementHelper.test.ts` pins the exact param set.
  - **Refactor (same session): the gate wiring was copy+pasted across the 4 call sites — extracted `shouldShowConnectionErrorToastForConnection` (async, dependency-injected: `getConnectionInfo` + `getSecurityMode` getters, so `syncSettlementHelper.ts` stays pure/unit-testable) in `syncSettlementHelper.ts`, which collapses the "resolve live settled transport via `isSyncTransportSettled` + run `shouldShowConnectionErrorToast`" block; new `SyncConnectionMode` type alias extracted from the inline union. All 4 sites (SyncConnectionContext handleSyncError + connect catch, ConnectionSetupScreen handleConnectionError + handleHandshakeAccepted catch) now call it. ALSO i18n'd the toasts: ConnectionSetupScreen had 11 hardcoded English strings — converted to `t('...')` (connection namespace; keys `connectionErrorToast`, `connectionCancelled`, `securityModeFailed`, `connectionRejectedToast`, `connectionFailedToast`, `reconnectedToast`, `reconnectFailedToast`, `unpairedToast`, `connectedToast` already existed; ADDED missing `failedToEstablishConnection` key). SyncConnectionContext already used `i18n.t('syncConnection:...')` — untouched. Verification: tsc clean; unit 28 suites / 333 tests (6 new for the async helper); integration 8 suites / 31 + 1 skip.
  - CRITICAL BUG CAUGHT IN REVIEW: the estimate payload field names. Engine serializes `SyncDataSizeEstimatePayload` with snake_case JSON tags (`estimated_download_mb`, `total_records`, `image_count`, `includes_images`, `image_size_mb`) but the app (and the mock server) read/wrote PascalCase (`TotalRecords`, `ImageCount`, `EstimatedDownloadMB`) — in production the estimate would always read as 0/0/0 and the dialog would NEVER appear. Fixed app reads + mock server emission + tests (Test 11 asserts `estimate.EstimatedDownloadMB` is `undefined`).
  - Themed dialog: reordered providers in `App.tsx` — `AppAlertProvider` now WRAPS `SyncConnectionProvider` (verified safe: AppAlertModal only depends on ThemeContext) so `useAppAlert()` works in SyncConnectionContext; replaced the RN `Alert.alert` fallback with the themed obsidian-glass dialog (icon `cloud-download-outline`, `blockBackdropDismiss: true`, Cancel→reject / Confirm→accept, `showAlertRef` mirror for the `[]`-deps listener).
  - Confirmation threshold: new pure helper `shouldPromptForSyncEstimate({totalRecords, imageCount, estimatedDownloadMB, limitMB, isInitialSync})` in `src/contexts/syncEstimateHelper.ts` — prompts ONLY when `estimated_download_mb > limit` (default 5 MB), `limitMB === null` = "Unlimited" → never prompt, empty (0/0) → auto-confirm, and `isInitialSync` → ALWAYS prompt for any non-empty estimate (bypasses limit). Initial sync detected via `ConnectionStateManager.getLastSync(getCurrentSource()) === 0` (no watermark yet — the watermark is only written at SYNC_FINALIZE). Setting persisted via `ConnectionStateManager.getSyncEstimateLimitMB()/setSyncEstimateLimitMB()/clearSyncEstimateLimitMB()` under AsyncStorage key `sync_estimate_limit_mb` (default 5, `'unlimited'` sentinel). `SyncSettingsScreen` gained a "Sync confirmation limit" dropdown card (1/5/10/20/50/100/Unlimited) via the shared `SelectPicker` + i18n keys (`estimateConfirmLimit`, `estimateConfirmLimitHint`, `unlimited`).
  - Verification: app `tsc --noEmit` clean; unit 28 suites / 333 tests green (13 syncEstimateHelper + 10 ConnectionStateManager + 6 connection-toast-helper new); integration sync suite 31 pass + 1 skip (syncService 14 incl. 4 estimate tests). Changes UNCOMMITTED — staged earlier sync-race work is still uncommitted too; user to decide commit split.
- Sync-Race Fix + Sync-Watermark Wipe Reset (2026-08-02): Diagnosed and fixed the "characters not appearing after pairing" sync failure; then added full-DB-wipe watermark reset and removed the legacy sync-timestamp alias. Three work items, all verified on-device + tests green:
  - (1) Settled-transport sync gate + abort safety net — root cause: auto-sync fired on the provisional plaintext ws:// pairing connection, then the ws→wss security upgrade tore the connection down mid-sync (buffered SYNC_DATA discarded, SYNC_COMPLETE dropped 4ms after listeners removed), orphaning `SyncService.currentSession` as 'in_progress' forever → every future sync logged "Sync already in progress, skipping" until app restart. Fixes: new pure helper `isSyncTransportSettled(connMode, persistedMode)` (`src/contexts/syncSettlementHelper.ts`) — TLS/cloud always settled, `unencrypted` only if user explicitly persisted it; `SyncConnectionContext.handleSyncConnected` is now async and defers `initiateSync()` until transport settles; new `SyncService.abortSync(reason)` (clears session/phase/buffer/serverRecordIds, rejects pending confirmation, emits `sync:aborted`) wired to `disconnected:sync` / `error:sync` / new `sync:connection_replaced` event (emitted by `ConnectionManager.createConnection` BEFORE tearing down an existing sync connection — the underlying WS 'disconnected' is suppressed there); Fix D: `handleSyncComplete` now `await sendLocalChangesSequentially(...)` so the phase machine advances deterministically; `SyncSettingsScreen` resets spinner on `sync:aborted`. Buffered server data is intentionally DISCARDED on abort (last-sync not advanced → engine re-sends everything = lossless recovery). Deliberately NOT reordered `disconnectConnection` (Fix C — CRITICAL blast radius, 25 callers/17 processes; documented follow-up). Tests: `syncSettlementHelper.test.ts` (9 unit), `sync.abort.test.ts` (3 integration w/ mock ConnectionManager emitting disconnected:sync/error:sync). On-device verification (emulator-5554, `ai.soulbits.chat.dev`): logcat shows gate "deferring sync until transport settles" (23:56:49.486) + "Aborting sync session: sync connection replaced" (23:56:49.649, 23:56:53.831); no stuck state; both sessions completed cleanly (0/0 because client DB was wiped but AsyncStorage lastSync survived — engine correctly had nothing newer; NOT a regression, expected incremental behavior).
  - (2) Full-DB-wipe resets sync watermark — root cause of "no data transferred after wipe": the app's SQLite wipe only removed the legacy `last_sync_timestamp` AsyncStorage key, while the per-source keys (`last_sync_timestamp:selfhosted`/`:cloud`) that `getLastSync()`/`setLastSync()` actually use survived → client told engine "synced up to <recent ts>" → engine returned 0 records. Fix: new `ConnectionStateManager.clearAllLastSyncTimestamps()` (removes all per-source keys) called from BOTH `wipeDatabaseCompletely` (Loading screen) and `clearDatabaseData` (Dev DB viewer). Per-source get/set, unpair/re-pair, app-restart persistence all untouched — only the full-wipe flows clear watermarks.
  - (3) Legacy sync-timestamp alias removed (Option B) — no long-lived installs from pre-per-source-migration, so dropped it entirely: `getLastSync` no longer falls back to `last_sync_timestamp`; `setLastSync` no longer dual-writes; `STORAGE_KEYS.LAST_SYNC_TIMESTAMP` deleted; `SettingsScreen` + `SyncSettingsScreen` "Last sync" display now read `ConnectionStateManager.getLastSync(getCurrentSource())`. Single source of truth = per-source keys only. Tests: `connectionStateManager.lastSyncReset.test.ts` rewritten (7 tests: per-source write/read, NO legacy fallback, wipe clears both, idempotent, credentials untouched); integration `syncService.integration.test.ts` + `sync.clock.test.ts` legacy-key seeds removed, `updates last sync timestamp on completion` now asserts legacy key is NOT written.
  - Verification: unit 26 suites / 295 tests green; integration 8 suites / 24 pass + 1 skip; `tsc --noEmit` clean; GitNexus detect_changes scope = wipe flows + settings screens' last-sync display only (risk HIGH inherent to destructive wipe flows). Changes UNCOMMITTED (4 sync-race files + 3 new files + wipe/legacy edits) — awaiting user decision on commit split.
- Google OAuth Environment Secret Wiring (2026-07-31): Dev/Prod OAuth client secrets are no longer hardcoded in tracked files. New `scripts/oauth-secrets.cjs` loader reads gitignored `client_secret_*.json` (search order: --file → secrets/<env>/ → secrets/ → repo root) and derives `.env` (APP_ENV/IS_BETA/GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID/APPLE_SERVICES_ID) + `android/gradle-secrets.<env>.properties`. npm scripts `oauth:dev`/`oauth:prod`; `android`/`ios`/`start`/E2E build scripts auto-load (with `--if-missing-ok` where optional). Android `build.gradle` resolves via -P flag → gradle-secrets file → '' (gradle.properties cleaned). Runtime: `cloud.ts` exports `APP_ENVIRONMENT` (env: dev|prod + label); `react-native-config.d.ts` typed `APP_ENV`; `googleSignIn.ts` warns when webClientId missing. CI unchanged (uses vars.* with -P priority; iOS regenerates .env per matrix entry incl. APP_ENV). `.env` untracked from git. Docs: `docs/OAUTH-SECRETS.md` + INSTALLATION.md update.
- Soulbits Cloud Config Convenience Features + Character Card Import (2026-07-30): Three user-requested features centered on the module config menu + Characters screen. (1) Endpoint auto-prefill: when Soulbits Cloud is the provider AND the app is cloud-connected, `ModuleConfigEditScreen.handleProviderSwitch` prefills `base_url` with the beta-aware `CLOUD_HOSTS.inference` (overrides the prod default baked into `PROVIDER_DEFAULTS.soulbitscloud.base_url`, which was the bug — beta builds showed the prod URL). Edit-mode never overwrites a stored value. (2) Module-filtered model dropdown: new `SoulbitsModelSelect` component replaces the free-text `model` field for soulbitscloud, loading valid models for the module type via a credential-less `createClient({inferenceURL})` against the public `GET /v1/models` catalog (5-min TTL cache, single-flight, never throws → static fallback on error/offline), plus a "Custom…" free-text override. Mapping in new `src/constants/soulbitsModels.ts`; service in new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts`. Shared infra: `FormField` `select` case now renders a real themed `SelectPicker` dropdown (was a disabled TextInput) — fixes existing select fields (reasoning_effort, aspect_ratio) too. (3) Character card import: ported harmony-link-private `utils/charactercard/` (types.go/png_parser.go/mapper.go) to a new pure-TS package `src/utils/charactercard/` (parser handles Tavern Card V1/V2/V3 from raw JSON + PNG-embedded tEXt/iTXt `chara`/`ccv3` chunks, base64-decodes; mapper → CharacterProfile + CharacterImage via `generateId()` UUID v7). Import service `src/services/CharacterCardImportService.ts` reads a picked file (RNFS), detects PNG/JSON, parses+maps+persists via existing repos (fully local, syncs via normal pipeline). CharactersScreen gained a header "Import Card" action (`@react-native-documents/picker` `pick`). Added `base64ToUint8Array` helper to `src/database/base64.ts`. i18n keys added to `moduleConfig.json` + `characters.json`. Tests: 6 new unit suites (jsonParser/pngParser/mapper/soulbitsModels/soulbitsModelsCatalog/base64) — 48 tests, full unit suite green (269 tests). tsc clean. NOTE: pre-existing eslint errors in ModuleConfigEditScreen (useCallback exhaustive-deps, unused moduleSpecificDefaults) + CharactersScreen (unused `Nav` type) are PRE-EXISTING (verified via git HEAD) — out of scope, left untouched. The `no-bitwise` warnings in the new binary-parsing code are inherent and don't fail CI. Manual/on-device verification deferred to user (build not run per workspace rules).
- Cloud-Mode Token Handling + Soulbits Model Defaults + TLS/UX fixes (2026-07-31): Six commits landed this session.
  - `353bf97 fix: Connection issue handling` — ConnectionSetupScreen cert-flow hardening: `hasSelectedSecurityModeRef` reset in `handleHandshakeAccepted`/`handleCredentialsCleared`/unpair/modal-abort; `handleCertVerificationFailed` → alert offering security-mode reset (i18n certResetTitle/Message/Confirm) then opens cert modal; "Reset Security Mode" button clears mode+resets UI+toast+opens cert popup; removed `setSecurityMode('secure')` dead-end. Root cause of phone TLS failure: app stores `harmony_server_cert` but never pins it; engine cert self-signed, SANs only localhost/127.0.0.1/::1 (no LAN IP) → "unknown certificate". Fix = re-pair in Insecure-SSL mode. Engine restarted with `SE_WSS_PORT=28443` (WSS/TLS); plain WS 28080, admin 28081.
  - `3167a8e feat: add speed dial button` — CharactersScreen FAB + modal replaced by RN-`Animated` speed dial: FAB rotates into ✕, two floating glass pills above it (Create Profile `testID=create-profile-option`, Import Character Card (PNG / JSON) `testID=import-character-card`), staggered open 220ms / close 180ms, backdrop/✕ closes; removed old modal + `createOrImport` i18n keys.
  - `7b3eb74 feat: simple profile picker` — CreateAIScreen links an EXISTING character profile instead of always creating a fresh one: profile selector + bottom sheet ("Create new profile" + all profiles); choosing one links the new entity to it (no unique constraint on `entities.character_profile_id` — verified valid), prefills Name/Personality, shows preview card with pencil → CharacterProfileEdit, hides photo/personality fields; alias conflict (`idx_entities_alias_unique`) → "Name already in use" alert instead of crash; `prefillProfileId` route param now honored.
  - `91fe902 fix: module pickers on create AI screen` — Advanced Settings: pickers were gated behind `hasAnyConfigs===true` (local-DB check) → empty DB showed dead-end "Connect to Harmony Link or Cloud…" warning. Deleted inline `ModuleConfigPicker` + warning block (~310 lines); 8 pickers now use shared `EntityModuleSelectorWithActions` (selector + ✎ edit + ＋ create → ModuleConfigEdit), always visible; `loadModuleConfigs` stable `useCallback`; `useFocusEffect` reload on return.
  - `5a10a51 fix: soulbits models defaults` — **no "soulchat" model exists on the live catalog** (`GET https://beta.api.soulbits.app/v1/models`, 20 models). Fake IDs removed: `soulchat-v1` (LLM fallback + `moduleDefaults.ts` default + `providerFieldSchemas.ts` placeholder), `soul-embed-v1`/`soul-tts-v1` (fallbacks), `whisper` (stt). Real replacements: LLM `qwen-35-9b`/`starfallen-24b`/`gemma4-meromero-26b-a4b`, embeddings `harrier-oss-v1-0-6b`/`qwen3-embed-4b`, TTS `harmonyspeech`/`kitten-tts-*`/`openvoice_*`/`chatterbox*`, STT `faster-whisper-tiny`/`faster-whisper-large-v3-turbo`, vision `qwen-35-9b`/`gemma4-meromero-26b-a4b`; default model `qwen-35-9b`. Added guard test: every fallback ID must exist in live catalog.
  - `5d5e7fe feat: convenience features for Cloud mode token handling` — see dedicated @Focus entry below.
- Cloud-Mode Token Handling design + implementation (2026-07-31): Engine (harmony-link-private) already injects the session PASETO into its seeded soulbitscloud row (`cmd/cloud_mode.go seedCloudSoulbitsCloudProvider`: seeds "Soulbits Cloud (default)" with `api_key=SE_INFERENCE_TOKEN`; `providers/soulbitscloud.go` switches PASETO-mode iff `api_key` starts with `v4.local.`). App-side gap closed: (a) **Inject on create** — `ModuleConfigEditScreen.saveProviderConfig` calls `injectSoulbitsToken({providerType, isCreate:!form.providerConfigId, providerConfig})` → sets `api_key` to current PASETO for NEW soulbitscloud configs only (updates/non-soulbits/standalone untouched); `handleProviderSwitch` also prefills `api_key` from `AuthService.getToken()`. (b) **Refresh propagation** — new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsTokenSync.ts`: `startSoulbitsTokenSync()` subscribes to `AuthService.on('auth:changed')` (login+register+refresh), bulk-updates all non-deleted soulbitscloud rows via new `updateAllSoulbitsCloudApiKeys(paseto)` repo fn (bumps `updated_at` so sync picks it up), THEN calls `SyncService.initiateSync()` to push to engine immediately (self-guards on in-progress/disconnected; connect-time auto-sync is the safety net). `syncCurrentToken()` one-shot on startup; `injectSoulbitsToken()` shared by UI. Wired in `AuthContext` useEffect (below DatabaseProvider → DB ready). (c) **Read-only credential UX** — `FormField` gained `readOnly?: boolean`: for password fields `editable={false}` + `secureTextEntry` locked + NO eye toggle + `contextMenuHidden`+`selectTextOnFocus={false}` (can't copy/reveal/break); soulbitscloud api_key rendered read-only when `isManagedSoulbitsApiKey` (same `v4.local.` prefix heuristic as engine). Tests: repo bulk-update (active rows updated, soft-deleted preserved), service (subscribe/unsubscribe, sync trigger, inject rules) — all green 279 tests/24 suites; tsc clean; GitNexus LOW on FormField (additive prop), medium detect_changes all internal to ModuleConfigEditScreen.
- Dev-mode detection audit + beta build commands (2026-07-31, informational): App knows dev via Metro `__DEV__` (compile-time) — gates logger severity, DatabaseTableViewer screen/menu/settings card, and `cloud.ts` `IS_BETA = __DEV__ ? true : Config?.IS_BETA`. FOOTGUN: exported `IS_DEV` alias = `IS_BETA` (beta-flavour), NOT `__DEV__`. soulbitscloud base_url prefill only when `cloudConnected` (mode==='cloud' && connected) — in dev connected to the local engine, creating a soulbitscloud config prefills PROD `api.soulbits.app`, while the model catalog (`soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts`) unconditionally hits `CLOUD_HOSTS.inference` (= beta in dev). Beta release build: `cd android; .\gradlew.bat assembleDevRelease -PE2E_DEBUG_SIGNING=true` (debug-signed, JS-bundled; only debug.keystore exists locally — no release keystore); output `android\app\build\outputs\apk\dev\release\app-dev-release.apk`; install `adb -s d608825c install -r <apk>`. `npm run android-prod` = prod flavor (IS_BETA=false) — NOT beta.
- Soulbits Cloud Config Convenience Features + Character Card Import (2026-07-30): Three user-requested features centered on the module config menu + Characters screen. (1) Endpoint auto-prefill: when Soulbits Cloud is the provider AND the app is cloud-connected, `ModuleConfigEditScreen.handleProviderSwitch` prefills `base_url` with the beta-aware `CLOUD_HOSTS.inference` (overrides the prod default baked into `PROVIDER_DEFAULTS.soulbitscloud.base_url`, which was the bug — beta builds showed the prod URL). Edit-mode never overwrites a stored value. (2) Module-filtered model dropdown: new `SoulbitsModelSelect` component replaces the free-text `model` field for soulbitscloud, loading valid models for the module type via a credential-less `createClient({inferenceURL})` against the public `GET /v1/models` catalog (5-min TTL cache, single-flight, never throws → static fallback on error/offline), plus a "Custom…" free-text override. Mapping in new `src/constants/soulbitsModels.ts`; service in new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsModelsCatalog.ts`. Shared infra: `FormField` `select` case now renders a real themed `SelectPicker` dropdown (was a disabled TextInput) — fixes existing select fields (reasoning_effort, aspect_ratio) too. (3) Character card import: ported harmony-link-private `utils/charactercard/` (types.go/png_parser.go/mapper.go) to a new pure-TS package `src/utils/charactercard/` (parser handles Tavern Card V1/V2/V3 from raw JSON + PNG-embedded tEXt/iTXt `chara`/`ccv3` chunks, base64-decodes; mapper → CharacterProfile + CharacterImage via `generateId()` UUID v7). Import service `src/services/CharacterCardImportService.ts` reads a picked file (RNFS), detects PNG/JSON, parses+maps+persists via existing repos (fully local, syncs via normal pipeline). CharactersScreen gained a header "Import Card" action (`@react-native-documents/picker` `pick`). Added `base64ToUint8Array` helper to `src/database/base64.ts`. i18n keys added to `moduleConfig.json` + `characters.json`. Tests: 6 new unit suites (jsonParser/pngParser/mapper/soulbitsModels/soulbitsModelsCatalog/base64) — 48 tests, full unit suite green (269 tests). tsc clean. NOTE: pre-existing eslint errors in ModuleConfigEditScreen (useCallback exhaustive-deps, unused moduleSpecificDefaults) + CharactersScreen (unused `Nav` type) are PRE-EXISTING (verified via git HEAD) — out of scope, left untouched. The `no-bitwise` warnings in the new binary-parsing code are inherent and don't fail CI. Manual/on-device verification deferred to user (build not run per workspace rules).
- Issue-2 Cloud Sync Rejection + UX Feedback (2026-07-30): Cloud-mode SYNC_REQUEST was rejected by HL because the device was never registered — the app's cloud connection intentionally skips HANDSHAKE_REQUEST (Cloud-Connection-Redesign Phase 4 "handshake trim"; PASETO at conduct-proxy replaces the HL handshake JWT), so the registration side-effect stranded in the handshake path never ran. Backend Fix #1 lives in harmony-link-private (extracted `findOrCreateDevice` shared by both handlers; handleSyncRequest now auto-registers+approves in cloud mode). APP-SIDE FIXES (this repo): added the missing `sync:rejected` consumers. The `sync:rejected` event was already emitted by SyncService (SYNC_REJECT→emit) and declared in `SyncServiceEvents` — only the UI listeners were missing, so a reject left `isSyncing=true` forever (initiateSync is fire-and-forget: it only awaits `sendEvent`, and no SYNC_ACCEPT/sync:error arrives after a reject). (1) SyncSettingsScreen.tsx: added `rejectedListener` → `setIsSyncing(false)` + `setCurrentSession(null)` + toast `syncSettings:syncRejected` (fallback to `syncError`); registered in the existing effect with matching `removeListener` cleanup. (2) SyncConnectionContext.tsx: added `handleSyncRejected` toast as defense-in-depth from any screen (e.g. auto-sync on connect); registered/cleaned alongside the existing `sync:completed`/`sync:error` handlers (`SyncService.off`). (3) i18n: added `syncRejected` key to BOTH `syncSettings` + `syncConnection` namespaces (en/ only — single locale dir). E2E regression guard `TestSyncRequestApproval` (soulbits-cloud-backend tests/e2e) sends a bare SYNC_REQUEST and asserts SYNC_ACCEPT. Build/test deferred to user.
- Soulbits API Client — dependency source fixed (2026-07-30): Client is now consumed as a real GitHub git dependency, NOT a local copy. Previously `package.json` declared `"file:../soulbits-api-client-js"` + an UNTRACKED `.npmrc` with `install-links=true` (forced a local-folder copy into node_modules; never touched GitHub). Now: `package.json` → `"git+ssh://git@github.com/harmony-ai-solutions/soulbits-api-client-js.git#518c9e8e9f36c9278489b861b3bed07d452ba3bc"`; `.npmrc` deleted; `package-lock.json` resolves git URL + commit + integrity hash. Required a `prepare` script on the CLIENT repo (`prepare: npm run build` → tsup) so npm builds the gitignored `dist/` on git-install (client only had `prepublishOnly`, which npm does NOT run on git installs — that's why dist was missing on first try). Client commit `518c9e8` (pushed) carries the prepare script. On a client bump: commit+push client, then re-pin the app's commit SHA + `npm install`. No npm publish needed.
- Soulbits API Client Adoption (2026-07-27): `CloudSessionService` now drives the session broker through the first-party JS client (`@harmony-ai-solutions/soulbits-api-client`, now a GitHub git dependency (see the 2026-07-30 note above)) instead of hand-rolled `authFetch`. New `src/services/cloud/soulbitsClient.ts` factory `buildSoulbitsClient({paseto})` builds the client **PASETO-only** (no `refreshToken`) → the client injects `Authorization: Bearer` but NEVER auto-refreshes on 401; a 401 surfaces to `CloudSessionService._doConnect`, which refreshes via `AuthService` (mirrors `AuthService.fetch` single-refresh-retry + `invalidate()`/`AuthExpiredError` on terminal). This keeps ONE persisted/broadcast credential for both REST and WebSocket paths (the client refreshes in-memory only with no read-back hook → would desync Keychain/WS). The app keeps its OWN poll loop using the client's `session.connect()` primitive — NOT `connectPoll` — to preserve the `requesting→provisioning→ready/failed` state machine, the per-poll UI feedback (`CloudProvisioningCard` elapsed timer), and the mid-poll `_cancelled` cancellation contract. `session.disconnect(sid)` replaces the disconnect RPC. `config/cloud.ts`: added `CLOUD_HOSTS.session` (= session-broker host, used as the client `cloudURL`); removed dead `AUTH_ENDPOINTS.sessionConnect/sessionDisconnect`. `authFetch.ts` is now ORPHANED (sole consumer was CloudSessionService) — left in place as a documented public-API wrapper. **Public API of CloudSessionService unchanged** → no consumer edits (`connect`/`disconnect`/`getStatus`/`getSessionId`/`getReadyAt` + `status` event + `CloudSessionStatus`/`CloudSessionInfo` types all preserved). Tests: `__tests__/cloudSessionService.test.ts` mocks `buildSoulbitsClient` + AuthService; 14/14 pass (added 401-refresh + disconnect-via-client cases). Stale GitNexus index (101 commits behind) — `detect_changes` listed 4 changed files (correct) but mapped symbols to `SyncConnectionContext` (a file never touched) — ignore as staleness artifact.
- Cloud Session Async Provisioning (Phase 11, complete 2026-07-25): Cloud session connection is now a fully async polling flow. `CloudSessionService` is an async state machine with states `idle → requesting → provisioning → ready → failed`. No `active` state at the service level — WS connectivity tracked by `useSyncConnection().isConnected`. The polling loop sends `POST /v1/session/connect` at the broker's `retry_after_ms` (500ms floor, 95-poll cap ≈190s) until the session is `ready` (200) or `failed` (503). The `BROKER_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS` client-side hack is removed — stale-session detection replaced by a consecutive-WS-failure counter (5 → fresh re-provision) and the broker's own lifecycle timers. A token-expiry pre-check runs before every cloud-mode WS dial. `canUseChat` gates chat/chat-list UI: cloud→`status==='ready'`, self-hosted→`isPaired`. `connectionStatus` produces mode-aware display labels. ConnectionSetupScreen shows a multi-stage provisioning card (Requesting → Preparing → Establishing → Connected ✓ / failed+retry) with elapsed timer and reduced-motion a11y. Coupled release: backend + app deploy together (no API versioning). See `docs/CLOUD-CONNECTION.md` for full detail.
- Test Flakeness Root Cause + Workaround (2026-07-24): unit DB suites (NodeDatabase / better-sqlite3 12.11.1 on Node 25) intermittently fail "Received function did not throw" on UNIQUE/FK/transaction-rollback when 2+ DB test files share a Jest worker — native-addon GC/timing contamination across :memory: DBs in one worker process. Deterministic under --detectOpenHandles (forces serial), intermittent in default parallel (bit 1-in-~6 observed runs). Extensive bisection RULED OUT: :memory: sharing, global UNIQUE disable, SQL-text/statement-cache collision, the transaction impl — failure is GC/native-timing at a file boundary, only reproducible with the real files (identical synthetic probe passes). FIX = isolation workaround, not a code cure: package.json `test:unit` = `jest --selectProjects unit --maxWorkers=16` (>= 12 unit files → 1 file/worker → no sharing → no contamination, verified 3/3 stable); `npm test` now = `test:unit && test:integration`; `test:raw` preserves old `jest`. ALSO fixed NodeDatabase to NOT apply PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL to :memory: (WAL is meaningless for in-memory DBs and better-sqlite3 HANGS outright on WAL+:memory: — reproduced standalone). If unit file count grows >16, bump --maxWorkers in package.json. Full analysis: docs/TESTING.md#known-issue-better-sqlite3-cross-worker-contamination.
- Project upgraded from React Native 0.83.1 → 0.86.0 and React 19.2.0 → 19.2.7 (2026-07-19). Required due to codegen incompatibility: `react-native-screens` v4.26.2 uses `React.ComponentRef<>` but RN 0.83.1's codegen parser only accepts `React.ElementRef<>`. Companion packages bumped to 0.86.0. The Gradle config (compileSdk 36, buildTools 36.0.0, Kotlin 2.1.20, NDK 27.1.12297006) was already compatible. Resolved a build-tasks ambiguity from product flavors (`dev`/`prod`) by adding `--mode=devDebug` to the `npm run android` script.
- Migration SQL Safety Guard + Stale-Column Investigation (2026-07-19): Investigated reported stale columns from migrations 007 (`audio_file` on chat_messages/conversation_messages) and 021 (`chat_template_kwargs` on openai/openaicompatible/openrouter provider configs). FINDING: both were already removed by LATER migrations — `audio_file` was dropped incidentally by migration 013's conversation_messages rebuild (its column list omitted it alongside the intended `vl_model_embedding`); `chat_template_kwargs` was dropped by the rebuilds in 030 (openai/openaicompatible) and 031 (openrouter). No cleanup migration was needed; the FIXME comments in 007/021 are stale leftovers. Added a forward-looking guard to the migration runner (`src/database/migrations.ts`, `assertMigrationSqlSupported` called at the top of `applyMigration`): migrations now FAIL FAST at apply time if executable SQL contains `ALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN` or `RENAME COLUMN` (unsupported on older-Android SQLite, breaks schema parity). Comment-stripping (`--` line + `/* */` block) ignores the FIXME documentation lines. Verified against all 32 existing app migrations (none trip; `DROP TABLE` / `RENAME TO` correctly allowed). Equivalent guard mirrored into harmony-link-private (Go); HL migrations 025 & 027 converted from DROP COLUMN to the `_new`-table rebuild pattern preserving HL's BLOB/TIMESTAMP/BOOLEAN types so the HL guard is unconditional.
- Universal Glassmorphism Overhaul Complete: All app cards now use Obsidian Glass — 45-55% opacity translucent fill with specular gradient borders and ambient neon glow shadows. GlassTokens extended with glowOpacity+glowRadius. ThemedCard is the single source of truth; 9 themes updated; ThemeCard and LandingCard use matching glass styling.
- Cloud Auth Layer (Phase 5) Complete: First HTTP layer + cloud auth for soulbits-cloud-backend. `src/config/cloud.ts` (CLOUD_HOSTS, WS_PATHS, OAUTH, AUTH_ENDPOINTS); `src/services/auth/` (tokenStorage Keychain `com.harmonyai.cloud.auth`, authFetch thin wrapper, AuthService singleton with fetch()/401-refresh-retry, login/register/loginWithGoogle/loginWithApple/refresh/logout/getProfile/getToken/getTokenExpiresAt/invalidate/resendVerification); `src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx` (status: loading|authenticated|unauthenticated). Provider wired between Database and SyncConnection. `getTokenExpiresAt()` from backend `expires_at` (NOT PASETO decode).
- Cloud Connection + Provider Mirror (Phases 6-7) Complete: harmony-ai-app now connects to Soulbits Cloud.
  - Phase 6 (cloud connection + session broker): `src/services/websocket/CloudWebSocketConnection.ts` (4th `ConnectionMode='cloud'`; RN built-in WS, standard TLS, PASETO via `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol: Bearer.<paseto>` against conduct proxy `/ws/sync`+`/ws/worker`; cert-error block dropped — ACM cert); `src/services/cloud/CloudSessionService.ts` (broker-only: POST /v1/session/connect spawn/claim + /disconnect grace; does NOT open WS itself); per-source lastSync (`ConnectionStateManager.SyncSource` + `getCurrentSource()` reads `connection_mode` AsyncStorage key); mode-branching in SyncConnectionContext (`/ws/sync`) + EntitySessionService (`/ws/worker`, 2 spots); PASETO-expiry handling — proactive timer (`CloudSessionService.scheduleProactiveRefresh` = `getTokenExpiresAt()-10min`, reschedule on refresh) + reactive (`CloudWebSocketConnection` onclose 1008/4401 → `AuthService.refresh()` → fail→`invalidate()`→AuthContext login).
  - Lifecycle wiring: AuthContext calls `cloudSessionService.connect()` on bootstrap/auth:changed IF `connection_mode==='cloud'`; `cloudSessionService.disconnect()` BEFORE `AuthService.logout()` (in AuthContext, NOT AuthService — avoids circular dep AuthService→cloudSessionService→authFetch→AuthService). EntitySessionService background AppState → `cloudSessionService.disconnect()`. Switch-warning Alert + spawning-spinner in ConnectionSetupScreen (`cloudStatus` state subscribes to cloudSessionService 'status').
  - Phase 7 (provider mirror): 7-0a split monolithic `providers.ts` (~3080 lines) into 16 per-file `<X>ProviderConfigRepository.ts` + `shared.ts` under `repositories/providers/` (NO shim; monolith deleted; all 4 importers updated). 7-0 migrated config-table family INTEGER→UUID PK (migration 031, mirrors HL 3-0) — full 7-tier cascade (models interfaces, 15 provider repos `id:string`+`createX` pre-gens `generateId()` UUID v7 via new `src/utils/uuid.ts`, modules.ts, entities.ts, SyncService/sync verify no Number() coercion, UI parseInt sites fixed in CreateAIScreen/EntityConfigEditScreen/EntityModuleSelector/AppNavigator). 4-way reconciliation per table. 7-1 added soulbitscloud (migration 032 UUID-native, `SoulbitsCloudProviderConfigRepository.ts`, model interface + ProviderConfig union member, providerFieldSchemas entry, SyncService 3 dispatch sites — lands the 6-3-deferred sync-dispatch).
  - Credential separation unchanged: cloud PASETO in Keychain `com.harmonyai.cloud.auth`; self-hosted `harmony_jwt` in AsyncStorage. `getTokenExpiresAt()` from backend `expires_at` (NOT PASETO decode — v4.local encrypted).
- Login UIs: `screens/auth/{LoginScreen,RegisterScreen,VerifyPrompt}` + mode toggle in `ConnectionSetupScreen` (self-hosted/cloud, `harmony_mode` persisted). New `auth` i18n namespace registered in `I18nContext`.
- Social Login: Google (`@react-native-google-signin/google-signin`, typed error discriminator, non-GMS fallback) + Apple (`@invertase/react-native-apple-authentication`, iOS-only AppleButton). Both handle 409 email-conflict messaging.
- Phase 8 (build flavors + CI) Complete: react-native-config@1.6.1 wired into src/config/cloud.ts (replaced ambient stub); IS_BETA centralized coercion (=== true || === 'true') — Android bridge surfaces JS boolean via BuildConfig reflection; iOS surfaces NSString from .env so cloud.ts coerces. Android productFlavors dev/prod (android/app/build.gradle: buildConfigField "boolean" IS_BETA, dev applicationIdSuffix ".dev", resValue build_config_package, debuggableVariants=["devDebug"], google-services plugin 4.4.2 + placeholder google-services.json both package names). iOS dev/prod is CI-driven (.github/workflows/build-release.yml dev/prod matrix: regenerates .env per entry + PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER override; single scheme, NO pbxproj/scheme surgery).
- Circular-dep lesson: 401-refresh-retry logic lives on AuthService.fetch(); authFetch.ts is a thin one-way wrapper (authFetch→AuthService→tokenStorage) — NO dynamic import.
- Credential separation: cloud PASETO in Keychain (`com.harmonyai.cloud.auth`); self-hosted `harmony_jwt` in AsyncStorage untouched.
- Provider Expansion Complete: xAI/Google/Anthropic provider support added across all module types. Model field unification (migration 000030). Dead code cleanup. 15 provider schemas in providerFieldSchemas.ts. 21 provider CRUD functions in providers.ts. ModuleConfigEditScreen supports all 15 providers. Module defaults include Google/xAI/Anthropic (maxtokens: 200).
